\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Lifecycle compute allocation}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{compute}

\p{Given lifecycle budget #{B}, a \strong{compute allocation} is a feasible
choice of component budgets}

##{
  B=(B_{\mathrm{roll}},B_{\mathrm{env}},B_{\mathrm{ver}},
     B_{\mathrm{upd}},B_{\mathrm{replay}},B_{\mathrm{ckpt}},
     B_{\mathrm{eval}}).
}

\p{This is an FTIP proposal paired with the lifecycle cost vector. A protocol
is feasible when its expected component costs do not exceed the corresponding
budgets. An exchange rate may be introduced for a specified machine, but the
component account remains available.}

\p{Rollout reuse \citef{miao2026when} moves work from generation toward
additional proposed updates. Trajectory extrapolation
\citef{chen2026lowrank} moves work toward checkpoints and predictors. The
optimal allocation depends on how each intervention changes independent
utility, not only its own step count.}
